  {
   "id": 669040,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"9\" type=\"1\">\n  <li>The functions <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> and <span data-math=\"g\">g</span> are defined by <span data-math=\"f(x)=8x+33\">f(x)=8x+33</span> and <span data-math=\"g(x)=2 \\cdot(1.2)^x\">g(x)=2 \\cdot(1.2)^x</span>. Which function eventually grows faster, <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> or <span data-math=\"g\">g</span>? Explain how you know.</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1333765,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"g(x)\">g(x)</span> grows faster because it is an exponential function."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333766,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"g(x)\">g(x)</span> grows faster because it is a linear function."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333767,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"f(x)\">f(x)</span> grows faster because 33 is greater than 2."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333768,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"f(x)\">f(x)</span> grows faster because 8 is greater than 1.2."
    }
   ],
